---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---
<Base title="Privacy · LapCraft" description="What this site and the app do with your data." path="/privacy">
  <section>
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px">
      <h1 class="display" style="font-size:2.4rem;margin:0 0 24px">Privacy</h1>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin:24px 0 8px">This site</h2>
      <ul style="color:var(--subtext);line-height:1.7">
        <li>Cloudflare Web Analytics counts page views. It sets no cookies and does not fingerprint you.</li>
        <li>PostHog counts page views and a handful of button clicks in cookieless mode. It sets no cookies and creates no person profile.</li>
        <li>The Buy Me a Coffee button in the footer is an image loaded from cdn.buymeacoffee.com, so that host sees your IP address.</li>
        <li>No account, no newsletter, no email capture.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin:24px 0 8px">The app</h2>
      <ul style="color:var(--subtext);line-height:1.7">
        <li>Laps, clips and settings stay in the app's private storage on your phone.</li>
        <li>Telemetry arrives from Gran Turismo 7 over UDP 33739 and 33740 on your own network.</li>
        <li>The app checks GitHub for updates on launch and opens release pages in your browser. It does not download or install anything itself.</li>
        <li>If you turn on event tags, the app fetches the GT championship schedule and, with a GT GridStats key, driver profiles.</li>
        <li>If you turn on anonymous usage sharing, the app sends event names and counts to PostHog: which screens open, clip saves, trim failures with a reason code, and import and share counts. It never sends your PSN ID, lap times, car or event names, or file names.</li>
        <li>The optional GT GridStats profile lookup sends only the PSN ID, using a key you paste in Settings.</li>
        <li>No accounts, no ads, no cloud backup. Anonymous usage is off by default.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>